1. A memory device, comprising:

a plurality of bank groups;

a first command/address bus and a second command/address bus, each coupled to the plurality of bank groups;

a toggle signal generator configured to generate a first toggle signal and a second toggle signal, wherein the first toggle signal and the second toggle signal are complementary to each other; and

control logic coupled to the first command/address bus, the second command/address bus, and the toggle signal generator, the control logic configured to alternate transmission of read/write commands and column addresses between the first command/address bus and the second command/address bus to the plurality of bank groups in response to the first toggle signal and the second toggle signal.
